; Roll a strength with a random spread
;
; Adds a random signed spread (#R$9CA8 with range ROLL_SPREAD) to the strength
; in A, for the fight in #R$9171. Observed over 64 rolls: the result is the strength
; plus 0 to 10 (mostly), saturated at $FF; a negative spread that does not
; underflow gives 0, and one that does underflow wraps (strength 0 gave 252 and
; 255). Looks like a bug in the original (inferred).
; .
; A Strength
; O:A Strength with the spread added
@label=RollStrength
c$9213 PUSH BC       ;
 $9214 LD B,A        ;
@isub=LD A,ROLL_SPREAD
 $9215 LD A,$0A      ;
 $9217 CALL $9CA8    ;
 $921A LD C,A        ; C: spread (signed)
 $921B ADD A,B       ;
 $921C JR NC,$9224   ; no carry: result in A
 $921E XOR A         ; carry: A := 0 ...
 $921F BIT 7,C       ;
 $9221 JR NZ,$9224   ;
 $9223 DEC A         ; ... or $FF when the spread was positive
*$9224 POP BC        ;
 $9225 RET           ;
